# Targets a doc PROPOSES but that do not exist yet. One name per line, with an
# expiry date and a reason. An entry here is a recorded intention; an unlisted
# stray is a lie.
#
# FORMAT:  <target>  <YYYY-MM-DD>  # reason
#
# The date is when the intention LAPSES, not when it was written. An entry with
# no date, or a malformed one, FAILS the gate immediately — that is deliberate,
# because an allowlist you can add to without a date decays into a graveyard, and
# every stale line is a hole in a gate whose whole premise is that an unlisted
# stray is a lie.
#
# A LAPSED entry warns, it does not fail. Failing on a date would red the gate on
# a day nobody chose, blocking a push for a reason unrelated to the change, which
# is how a safety device becomes an obstacle and gets bypassed. The warning makes
# the rot visible; you decide whether to build the target, drop the claim from
# the doc, or push the date out on purpose.

# name                     expires       reason
try_sage_smoke             2026-11-13    # docs/try-sage-docker-exploration.md PR 6 — proposed CI smoke check
try_sage_stop              2026-11-13    # same doc — proposed, never written; the doc now says so
try_sage_build_n_start     2026-11-13    # same doc — an option it explicitly recommends AGAINST
caprover_app_create        2026-11-13    # TODO.md open item — proposed CapRover wrapper
